// fixture-456: BUG-root-authority-kdl-transitive.md case B.
//
// A root direct dep ("softlink") shares its exact source (URL+ref) with a
// claim declared inside ANOTHER fetched dep's OWN milpa.kdl ("proptest",
// which itself declares "nim-z3" and "softlink" as git deps). Pre RFC
// origin-as-identity (docs/rfc-origin-as-identity.md), the old
// provenance_gate/TIER_* side-table left the BFS holding requirement edges
// whose candidate universe was never populated when the transitive kdl claim
// was deduped against root's own claim — collapsing resolution for
// "softlink", "proptest" itself, AND the UNRELATED sibling dep "nim-z3"
// (SOLVE-CONFLICT reporting every root term as unsatisfiable, even root's
// own softlink candidate).
//
// Expected (post RFC origin-as-identity S3a/S3b BindingResolver): resolves
// cleanly — all three deps ("proptest", "softlink", "nim-z3") present, with
// no collateral candidate loss.
name "t"
kind "application"
deps {
    "proptest" git=(url)"https://example.com/proptest.git" ref="main"
    "softlink" git=(url)"https://example.com/softlink.git" ref="main"
}
